For breast cancer follow-up, with detailed comparison to the radiation-therapy planning CT dated [date_1]:
(1) Very widespread coalescing ischemic gliotic lesions in the cerebral white matter (all showing increased diffusion and no enhancement), without neural parenchymal metastasis;
(2) Very widespread bone metastases involving all visualized bones (C2-4 vertebrae, the clivus, bilateral parietal bones, and both mandibular condyles), best seen on precontrast T1-weighted and FLAIR images;
(3) Dural involvement at the left parietal region (T2 hyperintense and enhancing), measuring 4 mm currently versus 10 mm on [date_1], with significant edema previously and complete resolution of edema. At this site, I cannot exclude recurrence; given this uncertainty, further examination would be recommended;
(4) Nonenhancing right mastoid and petrous apical cell effusions.
